-- THEOREM 8: ZERO-INTERNAL-WARRANT NON-INTERPRETABILITY THEOREM (`Warrants` -> `Empty`!)
-- External white-box observer sees internal cryptic wire value `cry-bobs (k , s) = bxor k s`,
-- where `k : Bool` is the secret per-wire gauge key and `s : Bool` is the true internal semantic bit.
-- We prove that for EVERY observed internal wire value `y : Bool` and EVERY claimed internal bit `target : Bool`,
-- claiming that the observation `y` warrants `s ≡ target` (`Warrants cry-bobs y (λ ks → snd ks ≡ target)`)
-- derives `Empty`! An adversary inspecting internal registers has ZERO epistemic warrant beyond I/O!
cry-bobs : Bool × Bool → Bool
cry-bobs ks = bxor (fst ks) (snd ks)
